{
  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "With only two completed experiments, the most critical uncertainty is the individual contribution of each modality. We know image-only (config_017, ViT-L) yields acc=0.227, and multimodal (config_001, scgpt+ViT-L, weighted fusion) yields acc=0.422. Testing RNA-only with the same scgpt encoder and singleprofile setting (config_011) directly decomposes the multimodal gain: if RNA-only approaches 0.40, the image adds little and we should focus on RNA encoder/fusion choices; if it is near 0.20–0.25, the image contributes substantially and image encoder improvements become high-value. This single experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty in the design space and will guide whether subsequent budget is better spent on image-side or RNA-side improvements. It is a clean, single-variable comparison to config_001 (only the modality is removed), making interpretation straightforward under the limited budget."
}

